Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 07:20:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: restore missing src/ai/analyzer.py and stop .gitignore
 from hiding it

- src/ai/analyzer.py was never committed: .gitignore contained a bare
  'analyzer.py' rule that silently excluded it from every git add,
  so the AI module referenced by src/orchestrator.py and
  src/ai/__init__.py never existed in the repository. This broke
  every import of the orchestrator (main.py once/run/status all
  failed before reaching collectors).
- Implemented TenderAnalyzer: calls local Ollama /api/chat with
  qwen3:8b, strips qwen3 <think> blocks before JSON parsing, retries
  once on transient failures, and raises clearly-labeled errors for
  connection refused / 404 model-not-found / timeout / malformed
  JSON instead of silently stubbing. Falls back to a labeled stub
  only when ai.use_stub_when_no_key is enabled in config.
- Also removed ~15 garbage .gitignore entries (/None, /Tender, /bool,
  /src/TenderAnalysis, etc.) left over from a prior broken script run.
- requirements.txt was missing truststore, which eis_zakupki.py
  imports unconditionally; pip install -r requirements.txt on a
  clean machine raised ModuleNotFoundError before any collector ran.
- README: documented that 'playwright install chromium' is required
  after pip install, since Fabrikant/RTS/TMK/Rosatom are
  browser-based collectors and fail with a clear (non-fatal) log
  message without it.
- tests/test_ai_analyzer.py: 7 new tests covering success parsing,
  <think>-block stripping, 404 model-not-found (raises, no stub),
  connection error with/without stub fallback, and malformed JSON.
